cmu-guidance-gps-help = A ground player must measure a target in rangefinder mode. Select their faction's report to program each guided round. Reports use the round's planet coordinate offset, expire after five minutes, and carry up to 15 tiles of error per axis. Reprogramming the same report does not reroll the error.
cmu-guidance-invalid-code = Laser codes must have four digits, a dash, then one digit (for example, 1111-1).
cmu-guidance-invalid-gps = Select a current ground report from your faction on the aircraft's target planet.
cmu-guidance-ammo-unavailable = That guided munition is no longer loaded.
cmu-guidance-gps-only = This shell only supports GPS guidance.
cmu-guidance-no-gps = This munition has no valid GPS target programmed.
cmu-guidance-code-mismatch = No matching laser signal on the aircraft's receiver code.
